Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sim): decide the #4107 snap per sample, so a floor
 reading both signs stays closed

A cut floor on the lattice reads about +-1e-12 at its samples, with both
signs. The per-edge snap put both ends of an edge between two such samples
of opposite sign on the samples, while that edge's own crossing stayed
mid-edge. The facet through the three was exactly collinear, push dropped
it, and the mesh opened by three edges: 45 open on the pin's box.

marching now reads a sample within NODE_SNAP of a step of zero as +0.0
(on_surface). cross returns the sample itself when one end reads exactly
zero, in place of the per-edge ratio. The pin
a_floor_on_the_lattice_reading_both_signs_stays_closed fails on main
(45 open) and passes here; #4107's unit tests still hold.

Fixes #4180

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
